@bank all
// Head writer W (playtest 1, 0.63.2; seat X's walk-up conversations): kind 'seek', the opener a crew member says when
// they've walked up and stopped beside you (the side chip, a bubble, then the chat card's first line if you tap).
// Addressed to you, 70 characters or fewer, a question or an invite. Tiers 1-4 (strangers don't walk up), plus the
// week-1 evening check-in (any tier) and someone leaving soon.

== seek
? tier=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. Got a minute? I've been meaning to find you.
- Oh good, it's you. How's your week going?
- {hi}! Saw you and thought I'd come over. Settling in?
- Mind if I stop a minute? My feet need a rest anyway.   #funny
- You look like you know your way now. Do you?
? tier=colleague
- {hi}, {nick}. Got a minute? How's it going?
- Just the person. Tell me something good about your day.
- You've been busy. I've seen you all over the ship. Sit a sec?
- There you are! I was going to come and find you anyway.
? tier=friend
- {nick}! Came over the second I saw you. How are you?   #warm
- There you are. I've been saving things up to tell you.
- Got a minute for me? Good. I've got news.
- I was just thinking I hadn't seen you today. Talk?   #warm
? tier=close
- {nick}. Come here. How are you, really?   #warm
- There you are. Everything's better with you about.   #warm
- I was looking for you. No reason. Just was. Got a minute?   #warm
? week1:true time:evening
- How was today, honestly? Got a minute to tell me?
- First week's a lot. Want to talk it through?   #warm
? leaving:soon
- Got a minute? I'm not here much longer. I wanted to say things.   #warm
- Before I go, can we talk a while? I'll miss this.   #warm
